From 91500316b05ee9bfcef3a14213b2b86ddb5ebff9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:46:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH v3 6/7] mailbox: sun55i: Add KUnit tests

Add 26 KUnit tests for the sun55i message box driver: the routing of
all 12 channels, sending on every channel, a message for a full FIFO
held until there is room (and dropped by shutdown), last_tx_done() and
peek_data() against the FIFO count, startup and shutdown dropping stale
messages (bounded by the FIFO depth), TX done by the write interrupt,
and the interrupt handler (spurious and disabled-channel interrupts,
empty FIFOs, several channels and routes in one pass, the drain bound,
the pending bit cleared after the drain, delivery outside the lock to a
client that replies from its callback, no crosstalk between channels).

The driver's register helpers are redirected with KUnit static stubs to
mock banks that model the hardware: reading a message FIFO pops it,
writing one pushes, and the interrupt status registers are
write-1-to-clear, a read pending bit only clearing once its FIFO is
empty.

---
Changes in v3:
- Moved after the drivers
- depends on SUN55I_MSGBOX (Sashiko)
- Register access is redirected with KUnit static stubs to mock banks
  that model the hardware: a FIFO read pops, a write pushes, and status
  registers are write-1-to-clear. No readl() on plain memory, so no
  architecture restriction and no endianness issue (Sashiko)
- The startup flush test now checks that the FIFO is drained; it
  passed through the failsafe before (Sashiko)
- New tests: drain before clearing the pending bit, full FIFO never
  written (message held in timer mode), TX done by write interrupt,
  delivery outside the lock
- Duplicate tests merged (routing is one table)
